[Music]  he famously promised  you'll never walk alone and over the  last year  this nation clung to those words  [Music]  jerry marsden with his unmistakable  smile  was the heart and soul of the band jerry  and the pacemakers  who made the song famous  [Music]  [Applause]  a hit in the 1960s mersey beat scene  they completed sellout tours around the  world  and were the first ever band to reach  number one in the uk  charts with their first three singles  the tributes were led by liverpool  football club  which adopted you'll never walk alone as  its anthem  jerry's words will live on forever with  us  the club's former chief executive  tweeted this video  of what he described as one of the most  treasured members of the lfc family  the news of jerry marsden's death was  confirmed by his agent and surviving  band members  who wrote losing such a legend is never  easy  we were all blessed to work with jerry  for many years  [Music]  jerry's heart was always in his hometown  in liverpool  where he remains a local icon jenny's  legacy will be  of course as one of the leaders of the  mersey beat era  and uh jenny was a a tough  man he was a tough lad and his youth and  he's a tough man  but he was also a very caring and loving  man it is the words of you'll never walk  alone you know  there is a golden sky isn't it and um  for many people that sky is a little bit  darker  jerry marsden died on sunday morning at  the age of 78  but not before he saw his famous song  reach number one once more  this time bringing the nation together  during a pandemic  when the words seemed more like a prayer  sadia chowdhury sky news

